{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Progressive Agent Autonomy.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Progressive Agent Autonomy.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"progressive agent autonomy progressive agent autonomy","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Progressive Agent Autonomy.md","fileName":"Progressive Agent Autonomy.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Progressive Agent Autonomy","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 12:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[DevOps Agent Safety and Autonomy]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["DevOps Agent Safety and Autonomy","agenticaifordevopsengineers.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Progressive Agent Autonomy.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Progressive Agent Autonomy.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"progressive agent autonomy progressive agent autonomy","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Progressive Agent Autonomy.md","fileName":"Progressive Agent Autonomy.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Progressive Agent Autonomy","heading":"Progressive Agent Autonomy","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Progressive autonomy grants authority in stages. At observe level, an agent analyzes and records results without changing the workflow. At suggest level, it can make visible recommendations. Controlled action permits limited operations such as opening a draft pull request or rerunning tests within policy. Semi-autonomous execution allows tightly gated remediation only after strong evidence and layered verification.\n\nAuthority remains revocable and bounded at every stage. Most implementations should stop at controlled action because production changes, security policy, and final merges carry consequences that require explicit human accountability.","tags":["baby"],"links":["DevOps Agent Safety and Autonomy","agenticaifordevopsengineers.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Progressive Agent Autonomy.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Progressive Agent Autonomy.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"progressive agent autonomy progressive agent autonomy","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Progressive Agent Autonomy.md","fileName":"Progressive Agent Autonomy.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Progressive Agent Autonomy","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[agenticaifordevopsengineers.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["DevOps Agent Safety and Autonomy","agenticaifordevopsengineers.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}